[b]Pick any building type, press one button, and it is queued in every state you can build it in (1, 5 or 10 levels at a time). No cheating, we just press the + button to add it to your queue.[/b]

Example: You just finished Electricity. Now every state wants a Power Plant, and the panel is a list of ninety states. So you click [b]+[/b]. Ninety times. Then again every time you take new land.

Now press [b]Build All[/b], once. And this works for any building type, not just power plants.

[h2]How it works[/h2]
In the construction panel you already use, open the [b]Build All[/b] section under Filters: a [b]1 / 5 / 10 level stepper[/b] and [b]one button[/b] to add to your queue.

Four key things:
[list]
[*][b]It obeys the Location filter.[/b] The panel's own [b]All / Domestic / Abroad[/b] selector decides where it acts. Whatever the list shows is what the button acts on.
[*][b]It can skip penalised states.[/b] Tick [b]Max. construction penalty[/b] and it only builds where this building's construction efficiency penalty is at or below your limit, so freshly conquered states stay out of the queue.
[*][b]It follows your sort.[/b] Sort by Earnings and it builds richest-first. It walks the list you are looking at, top to bottom, so you set the priority by setting the sort.
[*][b]It spreads levels evenly.[/b] Ask for 10 and every state gets its first level before any gets its second. Cancel halfway — or get dragged into a war — and your empire is evenly covered instead of three provinces deep.
[/list]

[h2]Not a cheat, not an autobuilder[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]It presses the game's own + button.[/b] Normal queue, cost, build time and funding.
[*][b]It cannot build what you could not.[/b] Any state the game would not let you click is skipped, like states already at their maximum level.
[*][b]It never acts on its own.[/b] Nothing happens until you press the button.
[*][b]It stops at 10,000.[/b] The button greys out once your queue holds 10,000 government constructions.
[/list]

[h2]Languages[/h2]

All eleven Victoria 3 ships: [b]English, French, German, Spanish, Português do Brasil, Polski, Русский, 简体中文, 日本語, 한국어, Türkçe[/b]. Terms come from the game's own text, so the button reads like the rest of the interface — but these are not native-speaker translations. [b]Post a correction and it goes in.[/b]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Game version 1.15.[/b]
[*][b]Achievement compatible.[/b]
[*][b]Save-safe.[/b] Add or remove it mid-campaign; it stores nothing in your save.
[*][b]Single-player.[/b] Untested in multiplayer, and not marked multiplayer-synchronised.
[*][b]Light on conflicts.[/b] It replaces one small interface definition, not the whole construction panel
[/list]

[h2]Feedback[/h2]

Post a comment if anything needs improving, especially translations.
